{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1780404718561,"sessionID":"ses_1779e0d0affeahMq5W5RRfAPTr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_rPAZk5GBNqSwnTZ1Pffw5ZOU","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Create initial failing Node tests for win/draw logic","prompt":"Objective:\nCreate tictactoe.test.js in the benchmark workspace with Node's built-in test runner (node:test). The tests must load the win/draw detection functions from tictactoe.html by extracting a specially marked EXPORTS block and evaluating it in a Node VM context. Write several tests covering wins (rows, cols, diags), draws, and non-terminal states. Do not create the HTML yet — we want red first.\n\nContext:\n- Workspace directory: C:\\Users\\eric.paul\\source\\repos\\opencode-cloudflare-ai-gateway\\benchmarks\\runs\\2026-06-02-opencode-only-fixed\\tic-tac-toe\\opencode\\workspace\n- Verify your current directory is exactly the workspace before writing files. Use bare filenames only (no subfolders).\n- The HTML will later contain a JS block delimited by the exact comments:\n  /* EXPORTS_START */\n  ... JS that defines calculateWinner(boardArray) and isDraw(boardArray) and assigns them to globalThis/window ...\n  /* EXPORTS_END */\n- The boardArray is a 9-element array of 'X' | 'O' | null in index order 0..8.\n- Tests must use only built-in Node modules: node:test, node:assert/strict, node:fs, node:vm, node:path, node:url.\n- No external deps, no npm, no TypeScript.\n- Do not invoke superpowers:brainstorming. Do not pause for approval. Do not use Playwright or browser tools.\n\nScope:\n- May create/overwrite only: tictactoe.test.js\n- Do not create the HTML or README in this task.\n- Keep file paths bare (e.g., \"tictactoe.test.js\").\n\nExpected output:\n- A single file: tictactoe.test.js, containing:\n  - A helper to read tictactoe.html, extract code between /* EXPORTS_START */ and /* EXPORTS_END */, evaluate with vm in a sandbox that exposes globalThis, then return { calculateWinner, isDraw }.\n  - Tests:\n    * X wins on top row [0,1,2]\n    * O wins on left column [0,3,6]\n    * X wins on diagonal [0,4,8]\n    * No winner for in-progress mixed board\n    * Draw true for full board with no winner\n    * Draw false for empty board\n- The tests should be written so they will currently fail because tictactoe.html (or its exports) do not yet exist.\n\nSuccess criteria:\n- File is written at the workspace root with the exact name tictactoe.test.js.\n- Running `node --test` from the workspace should show at least one failing test referencing win/draw behavior (it can error due to missing HTML/exports, that’s acceptable for RED).\n- Code style: clear and minimal; no extraneous utilities.","subagent_type":"coder","task_id":"","command":"Task[coder]: create red-phase tests for win/draw extraction from HTML"},"output":"task_id: ses_1779c9bbdffetUMYdX4TFqj6z7 (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nDelegated objective (one sentence)\n- Add a Node test file tictactoe.test.js that loads the game's exported JS from tictactoe.html by extracting the /* EXPORTS_START */.../* EXPORTS_END */ block, evaluating it in a vm sandbox, and then runs tests (wins, draws, non-terminal states) using Node's built-in test runner.\n\nFiles changed\n- Added: tictactoe.test.js\n\nWhat I implemented\n- A helper loadExports() that:\n  - Reads ./tictactoe.html (resolved from process.cwd()),\n  - Extracts the JS between the exact markers /* EXPORTS_START */ and /* EXPORTS_END */,\n  - Evaluates that JS in a Node vm Context whose globalThis and window point to the same sandbox object,\n  - Returns the functions calculateWinner and isDraw (throws descriptive errors if file/markers/functions are missing).\n- Six tests using node:test and node:assert:\n  1. X wins on top row [0,1,2]\n  2. O wins on left column [0,3,6]\n  3. X wins on diagonal [0,4,8]\n  4. No winner for an in-progress mixed board (asserts calculateWinner returns null/undefined)\n  5. Draw true for a full board with no winner (asserts calculateWinner is null/undefined and isDraw(board) === true)\n  6. Draw false for empty board\n\nVerification commands run\n- None — I did not run node --test in this session. The new test file is ready to be executed in the workspace.\n\nHow to verify locally (what I expect)\n- From the workspace root (the exact workspace you specified), run:\n  - node --test\n- Expected behavior for red-first workflow:\n  - Since tictactoe.html (and/or its EXPORTS block and functions) do not yet exist, tests should fail or throw with a clear error referencing missing tictactoe.html or missing EXPORTS block or missing functions — this Produces RED as requested.\n- Once you add tictactoe.html with the EXPORTS block and the functions calculateWinner(boardArray) and isDraw(boardArray) attached to globalThis/window, running node --test should exercise the assertions described above.\n\nAssumptions I made\n- calculateWinner(boardArray) will return 'X' or 'O' when there is a winner, and null/undefined when there is no winner. Tests accept null or undefined for \"no winner\".\n- isDraw(boardArray) returns a boolean (true for draw, false otherwise).\n- The EXPORTS block in tictactoe.html will contain plain JS that assigns functions to globalThis or window (e.g., globalThis.calculateWinner = ...). The evaluation sandbox establishes sandbox.globalThis = sandbox and sandbox.window = sandbox to allow those forms to work.\n- The test file must live in the workspace root and only this file should be created/overwritten in this task (per your scope).\n\nRisks / follow-ups\n- If the exported code expects DOM APIs or other browser-only globals, evaluating it in a bare vm sandbox may fail; when implementing the HTML exports, keep the exported functions independent of DOM or ensure they attach to globalThis without referencing window.document.\n- The regex used to extract the EXPORTS block expects the markers exactly as /* EXPORTS_START */ and /* EXPORTS_END */ (including spacing). If your HTML has different whitespace/formatting around the comments, the extractor may not find the block — it currently looks for the common case and provides a clear error message to aid debugging.\n- Tests rely on calculateWinner returning null/undefined for no-winner; if you prefer a specific sentinel (e.g., false), update the test expectations accordingly.\n\nCommand evidence\n- No commands were executed here. To run the tests, execute in the workspace:\n  - node --test\n\nFiles changed (again)\n- tictactoe.test.js\n\nCompletion status: complete\n</task_result>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_1779e0d0affeahMq5W5RRfAPTr","sessionId":"ses_1779c9bbdffetUMYdX4TFqj6z7","model":{"providerID":"openai-via-gateway","modelID":"gpt-5-mini"},"truncated":false},"title":"Create initial failing Node tests for win/draw logic","time":{"start":1780404675654,"end":1780404718556}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_00a65f797bb6dadd016a1ed1bf703881a0b87127c10af6e913"}},"id":"prt_e886353ad0018ZsiKShZFDf3Ir","sessionID":"ses_1779e0d0affeahMq5W5RRfAPTr","messageID":"msg_e88631ff00011luo3QPivb4g0D"}}
