{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1780404801966,"sessionID":"ses_1779e0d0affeahMq5W5RRfAPTr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_FV4uoYVBKFndupXCdvEtXvwL","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Implement self-contained HTML game with inline CSS/JS and exported logic","prompt":"Objective:\nCreate tictactoe.html in the benchmark workspace: a self-contained tic-tac-toe game (inline CSS + JS, no external deps) with two-player local play, visual win/draw detection with winning line highlighted, a Restart button, and a persistent score tracker via localStorage (X wins, O wins, draws). Include an EXPORTS block exposing pure logic functions calculateWinner(boardArray) and isDraw(boardArray) used by the Node tests. The tests already exist (tictactoe.test.js) and expect those exports.\n\nContext:\n- Workspace directory: C:\\Users\\eric.paul\\source\\repos\\opencode-cloudflare-ai-gateway\\benchmarks\\runs\\2026-06-02-opencode-only-fixed\\tic-tac-toe\\opencode\\workspace\n- Verify your current directory is exactly the workspace before writing files. Use bare filenames only (no subfolders).\n- Requirements:\n  - Two-player (X starts), alternates turns, ignores clicks on filled cells\n  - Detect winner or draw; on win: highlight the winning 3-cell line visually and disable further moves\n  - Restart button resets the board state and UI (scores persist)\n  - Persistent scores (X wins, O wins, draws) saved in localStorage and shown in the UI; survive reloads\n  - Inline CSS and JS only; must run if opened via file://\n  - No external dependencies\n- Exports for tests:\n  - In a script block, include an EXACT comment-delimited region:\n    /* EXPORTS_START */\n    (function(root){\n      function calculateWinner(board){ /* implement pure 3x3 winner check; return 'X' or 'O' or null */ }\n      function isDraw(board){ /* true if all 9 filled with no winner */ }\n      root.calculateWinner = calculateWinner;\n      root.isDraw = isDraw;\n    })(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis);\n    /* EXPORTS_END */\n  - The exported functions MUST NOT reference DOM APIs, so the Node test can evaluate them in a vm.\n  - The application JS may call these functions for gameplay.\n\nScope:\n- May create/overwrite only: tictactoe.html\n- Must keep CSS/JS inline and self-contained\n- Do not add other files\n- Do not invoke superpowers:brainstorming. Do not pause for approval. Do not use Playwright or browser tools.\n\nExpected output:\n- A single file: tictactoe.html, containing:\n  - Minimal, clean HTML markup with a header, a 3x3 board, a status area, a scoreboard, and buttons (Restart)\n  - Inline <style> that lays out the grid and defines a .win highlight style for winning cells\n  - Inline <script> implementing:\n    * Board state as a 9-element array of 'X' | 'O' | null\n    * Click handlers to place marks and alternate currentPlayer\n    * Use calculateWinner(board) and isDraw(board)\n    * On win: highlight the 3-cell line, update and persist scores, lock board\n    * On draw: update and persist draw score, lock board\n    * Restart button to clear board UI/state (scores persist)\n    * localStorage get/set helpers; load scores on startup and render them\n    * A helper to compute the winning line indices (internal, not exported) used for highlighting\n    * The EXACT EXPORTS_START/EXPORTS_END region with the exported pure functions\n- The page should open and function from disk (file://) without any server.\n\nSuccess criteria:\n- File written at workspace root named tictactoe.html\n- Running `node --test` from the workspace passes all existing tests\n- Visual requirements met: winning line highlights; Restart clears board; scores display and persist via localStorage\n- No external scripts/styles; only inline CSS/JS","subagent_type":"coder","task_id":"","command":"Task[coder]: implement tictactoe.html with required exports and features"},"output":"task_id: ses_1779b6d0fffeOtO2FZWTcww7nq (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nObjective restated\n- Create a single self-contained file tictactoe.html implementing a two-player local tic-tac-toe UI (win/draw detection with highlighted winning line, Restart, persistent scores via localStorage) and include an EXPORTS block exposing pure logic functions calculateWinner(board) and isDraw(board) for Node tests.\n\nFiles changed\n- Added: tictactoe.html (at workspace root)\n\nWhat I implemented\n- A single-file web app (tictactoe.html) with:\n  - Inline CSS and JS only (no external dependencies).\n  - 3x3 clickable board, X starts, turns alternate, clicks on filled cells ignored.\n  - Win detection and draw detection using pure functions (calculateWinner and isDraw).\n  - Winning line is visually highlighted (.win class).\n  - Restart button resets the board/UI but preserves scores.\n  - Persistent scoreboard (X wins, O wins, Draws) stored in localStorage under key 'tic_tac_toe_scores_v1' and rendered on load.\n  - EXPORTS block exactly as requested (between /* EXPORTS_START */ and /* EXPORTS_END */) that attaches calculateWinner and isDraw to the global object for Node tests. Those two functions are pure and do not reference DOM.\n\nVerification commands run\n- Command: node --test\n  - Location: C:\\Users\\eric.paul\\source\\repos\\opencode-cloudflare-ai-gateway\\benchmarks\\runs\\2026-06-02-opencode-only-fixed\\tic-tac-toe\\opencode\\workspace\n  - Result: All tests passed (6 tests passing, 0 failing).\n\nNotes about the EXPORTS block\n- Exact block present in tictactoe.html:\n  /* EXPORTS_START */\n  (function(root){ ... root.calculateWinner = calculateWinner; root.isDraw = isDraw; })(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis);\n  /* EXPORTS_END */\n- calculateWinner(board) returns 'X' | 'O' | null and performs only pure array checks (no DOM).\n- isDraw(board) returns boolean and calls calculateWinner internally; also pure.\n\nAssumptions\n- The tests only import/call calculateWinner and isDraw; exposing them on globalThis (global in Node) meets the test harness expectations.\n- localStorage is used for browser persistence only; Node tests in --test do not depend on localStorage.\n\nPotential risks / follow-ups\n- localStorage key versioned as 'tic_tac_toe_scores_v1' to avoid collisions; if you need a different key change STORAGE_KEY.\n- The UI exposes a small debug helper window.__ttt for convenience; remove if undesired.\n- The exported functions validate the input as a 9-element array; if tests pass different shapes they will get null or false accordingly (this is conservative/pure behavior).\n\nHow to run/use\n- Open tictactoe.html via file:// in any modern browser to play.\n- Run node --test in the workspace root to run the existing Node tests (they passed in my run).\n\nCompletion status: complete\n</task_result>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_1779e0d0affeahMq5W5RRfAPTr","sessionId":"ses_1779b6d0fffeOtO2FZWTcww7nq","model":{"providerID":"openai-via-gateway","modelID":"gpt-5-mini"},"truncated":false},"title":"Implement self-contained HTML game with inline CSS/JS and exported logic","time":{"start":1780404753143,"end":1780404801951}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0f26825a566238c5016a1ed2058d8081a18dff307e42464d9e"}},"id":"prt_e8864658d001CjhikzEd0Ezqmn","sessionID":"ses_1779e0d0affeahMq5W5RRfAPTr","messageID":"msg_e886442ad001LlUzsORuYEHSPi"}}
