{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1780404893153,"sessionID":"ses_1779e0d0affeahMq5W5RRfAPTr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_JsWRYYBxONINjg6iwPwb7Jw6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Add README.md with usage and testing instructions","prompt":"Objective:\nCreate README.md in the benchmark workspace explaining how to open the game, how to run the tests, what was scoped in/out, and any limitations.\n\nContext:\n- Workspace: C:\\Users\\eric.paul\\source\\repos\\opencode-cloudflare-ai-gateway\\benchmarks\\runs\\2026-06-02-opencode-only-fixed\\tic-tac-toe\\opencode\\workspace\n- Deliverables already present: tictactoe.html, tictactoe.test.js\n- Tests use Node built-in runner (node --test) and extract exports from the HTML between /* EXPORTS_START */ and /* EXPORTS_END */.\n- Do not invoke superpowers:brainstorming. Do not pause. Bare filename only.\n\nScope:\n- May create/overwrite only: README.md\n\nExpected output (README.md):\n- Title and 1-paragraph description\n- Open the game: instructions (double-click or open in browser, file:// OK)\n- Run the tests: commands (node --test), mention no npm install required\n- Implementation notes: inline CSS/JS, calculateWinner/isDraw exported via marked block for tests, localStorage key used\n- What’s in/out: Explicitly say no external deps, single HTML; mention accessibility minimal but reasonable; no AI opponents\n- Troubleshooting: If tests fail to find exports, ensure markers exist; Node >= 18 recommended\n\nSuccess criteria:\n- README.md written at workspace root with concise, accurate instructions","subagent_type":"coder","task_id":"","command":"Task[coder]: write concise README.md for game and tests"},"output":"task_id: ses_1779a552affevKo7a2qaaeq8TY (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nObjective (one sentence)\n- Create a README.md in the benchmark workspace that explains how to open the game, run the tests, what was scoped in/out, and any limitations.\n\nFiles changed\n- Added README.md (workspace root)\n\nVerification commands run and results\n- node --version\n  - Output: v24.14.0\n- node --test\n  - Result: All tests passed (6 passed, 0 failed)\n\nWhat I changed\n- Created README.md at:\n  C:\\Users\\eric.paul\\source\\repos\\opencode-cloudflare-ai-gateway\\benchmarks\\runs\\2026-06-02-opencode-only-fixed\\tic-tac-toe\\opencode\\workspace\\README.md\n\nSummary of README contents (high level)\n- Title and one-paragraph description of the single-file Tic Tac Toe app.\n- How to open the game: double-click tictactoe.html or open via file://; option to serve from a local static server.\n- How to run the tests: use the Node built-in test runner (node --test), no npm install required.\n- Explanation of how tests work: the test file reads tictactoe.html and extracts the JavaScript between /* EXPORTS_START */ and /* EXPORTS_END */; that snippet is evaluated in a Node vm sandbox where globalThis/window point to the same object; tests expect calculateWinner and isDraw to be attached to global/window.\n- Implementation notes: single HTML with inline CSS/JS; calculateWinner and isDraw live in the EXPORTS block; localStorage key used: \"tic_tac_toe_scores_v1\"; basic accessibility (role=\"grid\", aria-label), minimal UI.\n- Scope in/out: no external deps, single HTML, no AI opponent, not a production-level accessibility implementation.\n- Troubleshooting: guidance for missing EXPORTS markers, exported function names, and Node version recommendation (Node >= 18 recommended).\n\nFacts vs. assumptions\n- Facts:\n  - tictactoe.html is a single HTML file containing inline CSS/JS.\n  - The file includes the exact EXPORTS markers: /* EXPORTS_START */ and /* EXPORTS_END */.\n  - calculateWinner and isDraw are defined between those markers and attached to global/window.\n  - The app persists scores to localStorage using STORAGE_KEY = 'tic_tac_toe_scores_v1'.\n  - tictactoe.test.js reads the HTML, extracts the EXPORTS block, evaluates it in a vm sandbox, and asserts those two functions.\n  - node --test ran in this workspace and all tests passed.\n- Assumptions (stated):\n  - README recommends Node >= 18 for compatibility; this is conservative guidance (actual environment used Node v24 which works fine).\n  - The app's accessibility is described as \"minimal but reasonable\" — this is a qualitative assessment, not a formal audit.\n\nRemaining risks / follow-up\n- If the EXPORTS markers or exported function names are renamed or moved, the Node tests will fail; keep the EXPORTS block and exported names unchanged unless you update the test harness.\n- If you intend to add more testable helpers, follow the same pattern (place pure functions in the EXPORTS block and attach them to global/window).\n- If you need tests to run in earlier Node versions, verify vm and test runner support in that version.\n\nNotes\n- I did not invoke the brainstorming skill (per your request).\n- README.md was added only; no other files changed.\n\nCompletion status: complete\n</task_result>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_1779e0d0affeahMq5W5RRfAPTr","sessionId":"ses_1779a552affevKo7a2qaaeq8TY","model":{"providerID":"openai-via-gateway","modelID":"gpt-5-mini"},"truncated":false},"title":"Add README.md with usage and testing instructions","time":{"start":1780404824794,"end":1780404893147}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0735fad40b73b9c1016a1ed254592881a2b0897ccba1e9bfb0"}},"id":"prt_e88659967001VRU3cWTjWlz2RC","sessionID":"ses_1779e0d0affeahMq5W5RRfAPTr","messageID":"msg_e8865898e001RCnIO261hkLzIu"}}
