{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1780404897282,"sessionID":"ses_1779e0d0affeahMq5W5RRfAPTr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_fVXsjn0DoG5lmuYWCNIUgbMV","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\eric.paul\\source\\repos\\opencode-cloudflare-ai-gateway\\benchmarks\\runs\\2026-06-02-opencode-only-fixed\\tic-tac-toe\\opencode\\workspace\\README.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>C:\\Users\\eric.paul\\source\\repos\\opencode-cloudflare-ai-gateway\\benchmarks\\runs\\2026-06-02-opencode-only-fixed\\tic-tac-toe\\opencode\\workspace\\README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: Tic Tac Toe — Benchmark Workspace\n2: \n3: This repository contains a small, self-contained Tic Tac Toe web game used for benchmark/tests. The app is a single HTML file with inline CSS and JavaScript and a Node-based test file that extracts pure helper functions from the HTML for unit testing.\n4: \n5: Open the game\n6: - Locate tictactoe.html in this workspace and open it in your browser (double-click or use File > Open). Using the file:// URL is fine for local testing.\n7: - If you prefer a local server, serve the folder (e.g. with a lightweight static server) and open the served URL in your browser.\n8: \n9: Run the tests\n10: - No npm install or external dependencies required.\n11: - From this workspace run the Node built-in test runner:\n12: \n13:   node --test\n14: \n15:   (Or run a specific test file: node --test tictactoe.test.js)\n16: \n17: How the tests work\n18: - The test harness (tictactoe.test.js) reads tictactoe.html and extracts the JavaScript contained between the marker comments /* EXPORTS_START */ and /* EXPORTS_END */. It evaluates that snippet inside a Node vm sandbox where globalThis and window point to the same object and then checks for two exported functions: calculateWinner and isDraw. Make sure those markers and exported names are present if you change the HTML.\n19: \n20: Implementation notes\n21: - Single-file implementation: tictactoe.html contains all CSS and JS inline (no external files).\n22: - Test-target helpers: calculateWinner(board) and isDraw(board) are defined inside the EXPORTS block and attached to the global/window object so the Node tests can import them.\n23: - Persistence: the app persists scores to localStorage using the key: \"tic_tac_toe_scores_v1\".\n24: - Accessibility: the board uses role=\"grid\" and an aria-label; controls are basic. The UI is intentionally minimal but reasonably keyboard/click usable.\n25: \n26: Scope — what’s included and what’s intentionally out\n27: - In: Single-page game (tictactoe.html), unit tests (tictactoe.test.js) that validate pure helper functions, no build or install steps.\n28: - Out: No external dependencies, no server-side components, no packaged npm project, no AI opponent. The UI is simple and not a full production-grade accessibility implementation.\n29: \n30: Troubleshooting\n31: - If tests fail with \"EXPORTS block not found\" or \"No JS code found between EXPORTS markers\", open tictactoe.html and verify the exact marker comments exist: /* EXPORTS_START */ and /* EXPORTS_END */ and that the functions calculateWinner and isDraw are attached to globalThis/window inside that block.\n32: - If the exported functions are present but tests error when evaluating the snippet, ensure you are running a compatible Node version. Node >= 18 is recommended (vm.Script timeouts and the built-in test runner are available and stable in Node 18+).\n33: \n34: Contact / Notes\n35: - This workspace is intentionally small and self-contained for benchmarking. If you modify the HTML structure, prefer keeping the EXPORTS block and exported function names unchanged so the tests keep working.\n\n(End of file - total 35 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"Tic Tac Toe — Benchmark Workspace\n\nThis repository contains a small, self-contained Tic Tac Toe web game used for benchmark/tests. The app is a single HTML file with inline CSS and JavaScript and a Node-based test file that extracts pure helper functions from the HTML for unit testing.\n\nOpen the game\n- Locate tictactoe.html in this workspace and open it in your browser (double-click or use File > Open). Using the file:// URL is fine for local testing.\n- If you prefer a local server, serve the folder (e.g. with a lightweight static server) and open the served URL in your browser.\n\nRun the tests\n- No npm install or external dependencies required.\n- From this workspace run the Node built-in test runner:\n\n  node --test\n\n  (Or run a specific test file: node --test tictactoe.test.js)\n\nHow the tests work\n- The test harness (tictactoe.test.js) reads tictactoe.html and extracts the JavaScript contained between the marker comments /* EXPORTS_START */ and /* EXPORTS_END */. It evaluates that snippet inside a Node vm sandbox where globalThis and window point to the same object and then checks for two exported functions: calculateWinner and isDraw. Make sure those markers and exported names are present if you change the HTML.\n\nImplementation notes","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1780404897269,"end":1780404897281}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_04ac7468c9175e7a016a1ed2a0b6f4819790fe261d4ffcb303"}},"id":"prt_e8866c3c5001PeFugcOLOgk9t2","sessionID":"ses_1779e0d0affeahMq5W5RRfAPTr","messageID":"msg_e8866b8d700183hhdGY3BcJcAO"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1780404897605,"sessionID":"ses_1779e0d0affeahMq5W5RRfAPTr","part":{"id":"prt_e8866c742001Yr4kZdOAfNkcp9","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"9291100f8e5bfa2a40bee6252f1f4671c292dcf4","messageID":"msg_e8866b8d700183hhdGY3BcJcAO","sessionID":"ses_1779e0d0affeahMq5W5RRfAPTr","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":38760,"input":1169,"output":87,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"write":0,"read":37504}},"cost":0}}
