{"type":"text","timestamp":1780404929307,"sessionID":"ses_1779e0d0affeahMq5W5RRfAPTr","part":{"id":"prt_e88671fd9001CaJpca6isdDSkj","messageID":"msg_e886707db001QconDlp2vLZsIc","sessionID":"ses_1779e0d0affeahMq5W5RRfAPTr","type":"text","text":"Using superpowers: writing-plans to create the implementation plan\n\nPlan summary (TDD, bite-sized, no extra files created due to benchmark constraints):\n- Files:\n  - Create: tictactoe.test.js (Node built-in tests that extract exports from HTML)\n  - Create: tictactoe.html (single self-contained game; inline CSS/JS; includes EXPORTS block)\n  - Create: README.md (usage + test instructions)\n- TDD steps:\n  1) RED: Add failing tests in tictactoe.test.js that:\n     - Read tictactoe.html\n     - Extract code between /* EXPORTS_START */ … /* EXPORTS_END */\n     - Evaluate in node:vm; expect calculateWinner/isDraw present\n     - Assert wins (rows, cols, diags), draw/no-draw cases\n     Run node --test → expect failures (HTML missing)\n  2) GREEN: Implement tictactoe.html:\n     - 3x3 grid; two-player turn-taking; ignore filled cells\n     - calculateWinner(board) and isDraw(board) pure functions inside EXPORTS block, assigned to globalThis/window\n     - Highlight winning line; disable board when game over\n     - Restart button clears board (scores persist)\n     - Scores persist in localStorage (X, O, Draws)\n     Run node --test → expect all tests pass\n  3) README.md with how to open, how to run tests, scope, and notes\n\nUsing superpowers: test-driven-development to drive implementation red → green\n\nExecution and delegation:\n- Dispatched coder to add RED tests (tictactoe.test.js)\n- Ran node --test to confirm RED\n- Dispatched coder to implement tictactoe.html with required EXPORTS and UI\n- Ran node --test to confirm GREEN\n- Dispatched coder to add README.md\n\nFresh verification before completion (evidence, not claims):\n- node --test from workspace (first run, RED expected):\n  - 6 tests, 0 pass, 6 fail\n  - Error: Could not read tictactoe.html (expected, HTML not yet created)\n- After implementation, node --test (GREEN):\n  - tests 6, suites 0, pass 6, fail 0, duration ~96ms\n- Re-run node --test again (fresh evidence):\n  - tests 6, pass 6, fail 0, duration ~96ms\n- Spot-check tictactoe.html for required markers and persistence:\n  - Found /* EXPORTS_START */ and /* EXPORTS_END */\n  - Found localStorage get/set for score persistence\n\nDeliverables created at workspace root:\n- tictactoe.html\n- tictactoe.test.js\n- README.md\n\nNotes on implementation:\n- Exports block is pure and exactly delimited for tests:\n  /* EXPORTS_START */\n  (function(root){\n    function calculateWinner(board){ /* returns 'X' | 'O' | null */ }\n    function isDraw(board){ /* true iff all filled and no winner */ }\n    root.calculateWinner = calculateWinner;\n    root.isDraw = isDraw;\n  })(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis);\n  /* EXPORTS_END */\n- UI: 3x3 grid, click-to-play, X starts, win-line highlight (.win), restart button, scoreboard\n- Persistence: localStorage key tic_tac_toe_scores_v1 (X, O, Draws)\n- Inline CSS/JS only; opens via file://; no external deps\n\nHow to run:\n- Open game: double-click tictactoe.html (file:// URL)\n- Run tests: node --test\n\nDone.","time":{"start":1780404920281,"end":1780404929306},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0e9a10dd3024b193016a1ed2b84aec8194b384ba8f9fd04b67"}}}}
